# Every text file in this repository is stored and checked out with LF endings,
# including the .bat launchers, which cmd.exe runs perfectly well that way.
#
# This exists because a batch of edits made through a tool that rewrote whole
# files converted three of them from LF to CRLF. Nothing broke - PowerShell,
# the browser and cmd.exe all accept either - but every line of those files
# showed as changed, which turned a 117-line diff into an 1867-line one and
# pointed git blame at the wrong commit for the entire file.
#
# eol=lf rather than just text=auto: normalising on commit alone would still let
# a working copy fill with CRLF and produce the same noise on the next edit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Detected as binary anyway; named so nothing can decide otherwise.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pfx binary
*.cer binary
